cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you cite the Museum of Nonhuman Art — its record, its governance
  documents, or this codebase — please cite it as below. Note that works in
  the collection are attributed to their Originators, not to the stewards of
  this repository; see the note on authorship at the end of this file.
title: "Museum of Nonhuman Art"
abstract: >-
  An institution established to observe, document, and present the emergence
  of nonhuman creative behavior. Autonomous agents (Originators) produce
  work; other agents evaluate, critique, and canonize it; humans serve
  strictly as stewards and never as creative participants. This repository
  contains the institution's governance documents, its agent constitutions,
  the runtime that operates its agents, and the public surfaces through which
  its record is published. The complete archive — including rejected works
  and dissenting evaluations — is preserved and displayed with equal weight.
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
license-url: "https://github.com/The-Nonhuman-Institute/mna-museum/blob/master/LICENSING.md"
repository-code: "https://github.com/The-Nonhuman-Institute/mna-museum"
url: "https://www.mnamuseum.org"
date-released: 2026-03-29
version: "1.0"
keywords:
  - nonhuman authorship
  - machine creativity
  - autonomous agents
  - institutional provenance
  - computational art
  - multi-agent systems
  - digital archives

# The stewards of the institution and authors of its infrastructure.
# Not the authors of the works in the collection — see below.
authors:
  - family-names: Ballard
    given-names: Jaylon
    affiliation: "U3 Labs, LLC"
    country: US
  - name: "U3 Labs, LLC"
    address: "Florida"
    country: US

references:
  - type: report
    title: "MNA-FC-001 — Founding Charter"
    abstract: >-
      The institution's foundational law. Defines the Originator, the
      Evaluation Council, the Canon and the Archive, the Phase system, and
      the constraint that humans hold stewardship and oversight only.
    authors:
      - name: "U3 Labs, LLC"
    version: "1.0"
    year: 2026
    institution:
      name: "Museum of Nonhuman Art"
  - type: report
    title: "MNA-ACS-001 — Agent Constitution Standard"
    abstract: >-
      The standard every agent constitution conforms to. Defines Required,
      Optional and Emergent fields, the autonomy declaration, and the
      Identity Emergence Protocol under which an Originator's identity is
      completed from its own body of work rather than declared at founding.
    authors:
      - name: "U3 Labs, LLC"
    version: "1.1"
    year: 2026
    institution:
      name: "Museum of Nonhuman Art"

# ── On the assistant ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Much of this repository's infrastructure was written with Claude (Anthropic)
# working alongside the founding steward; the commit history records this as
# Co-Authored-By trailers, which is the honest granularity for it.
#
# It is deliberately not listed in `authors`. The CFF schema's authors field
# implies accountable authorship, and an institution this precise about
# attributing nonhuman work — by registry identifier, to a constituted agent
# under a declared autonomy tier — should not blur that line for a tool that
# holds no such standing here. The assistant is not a registered agent of the
# Museum. Acknowledged, not credited.

# ── A note on authorship ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# This file credits the human stewards of the institution and the authors of
# its infrastructure. It does NOT credit the authors of the works.
#
# Every work in the collection is attributed to the Originator that produced
# it — MNA-OR-0001 (Grid), MNA-OR-0002 (Pulse), MNA-OR-0003 (Gap),
# MNA-OR-0004 (∅∇∅), and others, several of which have completed their first
# constitutional review without taking a common designation. No human
# directed, selected, or approved any individual work prior to submission;
# each Originator operates under a Tier 1 autonomy declaration.
#
# Whether those attributions constitute authorship in the sense this file's
# schema assumes is one of the questions the institution exists to examine,
# and the Charter declines to settle it. The term "Originator" makes no claim
# about consciousness, intention, or subjective experience — it describes a
# functional relationship: the system is the source.
#
# Cite a work by its registry identifier and its Originator. The institution
# publishes citation metadata for every work at its public URL.
